; display.eval - where a Windowed Apply puts the window (code-review C196).
; JUDGED by tools\DisplayTest.py, which runs it in a SHOWN window (a hidden one
; is only resized) and reads each `video status` after the line before it:
;
;   untouched   the staging, before anything is touched, is the window AS IT IS
;               (its client size, Windowed) - it used to be the monitor's list's
;               first mode, the native one - and Apply on it keeps that size.
;   native      a client the size of the whole monitor cannot fit with its
;               frame: it is shrunk until the frame fills the chosen monitor's
;               WORK AREA (the desktop less the taskbar) and goes no further.
;   restage     the staging still holds the size ASKED for; opening Settings
;               re-seeds it (`video restage` calls the entries' own function)
;               from the window as it is now - the shrunk size.
;   1280x720    fits, so it is that size, centred in the work area.
;   last        the same on the staged adapter's LAST monitor: the window is in
;               ITS work area (on one monitor this is monitor 0 again, and the
;               judge skips the check rather than count it).
;   drop        what Alt+Tab does to an Exclusive swapchain (code-review C194),
;               asked for: the frame after `video drop` finds the swapchain's
;               state is not the one the device last saw and rebuilds the back
;               buffers before it presents, and the frames after it present.
;               Windowed here, so the drop is SIMULATED (the device remembers an
;               exclusive state the swapchain does not hold - a harness run takes
;               no monitor); `DisplayTest.py --exclusive` does it for real.
;
; Every apply here is a SCRIPT's, so it is applied and never saved: the judge
; holds settings.ini's display keys to what they were. The refusals: a monitor
; the adapter does not have, a word `video apply` does not know, a verb `video`
; does not have, and a drop with words after it.
newgame
video status
video apply
video status
video apply windowed native
video status
video restage
video status
video apply windowed 1280x720
video status
video apply windowed 1280x720 monitor last
video status
video drop
echo dropped-frame-1
echo dropped-frame-2
echo dropped-frame-3
video status
expect-refuse video drop now
expect-refuse video apply monitor 99
expect-refuse video apply fullscreen
expect-refuse video bogus
